WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.070
- [Narrator] The House Select Committee

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.840
investigating the Capitol riot,

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.780
wrapped its first series of
public hearings on Thursday

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.640
- We have far more evidence to share

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.430
with the American people
and more to gather.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.410
- The committee was formed in the wake

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.043
of the January 6th, 2021
attack on the Capitol,

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.890
in order to find out what happened.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.450
- [Narrator] The eight televised hearings

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.910
aimed to make the case that
former President Donald Trump

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.260
was accountable for the attack

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.440
and that it was the result of
a multi-pronged conspiracy.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.330
Trump has said he's done nothing wrong,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.690
and has called the committee
a "partisan witch hunt."

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.520
The Journal's, Scott Patterson explains

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.250
how the committee has presented
evidence they say shows

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.660
that Trump failed to intervene

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.580
after setting the stage for the riot.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.280
Promoted baseless accusations
of election fraud.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.703
And led a pressure campaign
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.630
The committee's latest prime time session

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.610
zeroed in on Trump's activities inside

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.460
the White House during the 187 minutes

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.000
after he gave his speech at
the Ellipse on January 6th.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.640
According to live and recorded
testimony on Thursday,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.590
Trump spent more than two and a half hours

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.020
in front of a television
in his private dining room

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.730
as rioters breached the Capitol.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:12.210
- What people were really
asking President Trump to do,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.040
including his own family,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.770
and top officials in the White House,

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.680
was for him to put out a
statement to the rioters

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.620
to stop and leave the Capitol building.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.530
- If the president had
wanted to make a statement

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.540
and address the American people,

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.690
he could have been on
camera almost instantly.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.130
- [Narrator] The committee
also played outtakes

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.180
from a video recorded

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.820
at the White House on January 7th, 2021,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.410
which showed that the former president

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.110
still refused to concede
that he lost the election.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.270
- This election is now over.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.490
Congress has certified the results.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.810
I don't wanna say the elections over.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.160
I just wanna say Congress
has certified the results,

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.560
without saying the election's over, okay?

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.820
- [Scott] It was the first
time in the history of

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.140
the United States that we did not

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.233
have a peaceful transfer of power.

00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:01.350
- [Woman] Traitor, traitor!

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.310
- [Narrator] Cassidy Hutchinson,

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.220
a one time aide to White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.810
testified in an earlier hearing

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.000
that Trump knew that his
supporters were armed

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.580
when he urged them to
march to the Capitol.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.230
Hutchinson said Trump was briefed about

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.970
the presence of weapons at the rally,

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.770
but was concerned that magnetometers

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.110
were keeping supporters from attending.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.760
- I overheard the
president say something to

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.417
the effect of, you know,

00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:25.200
"I don't effing care
that they have weapons.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.440
They're not here to hurt me,
take the effing mags away."

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.557
- Despite knowing all this he
stands before them and says,

00:02:32.557 --> 00:02:34.350
"Go to the Capitol."

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.330
- The committee played
never before seen footage

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.710
of rioters breaching the building

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.510
as officers brace for the assault.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.820
- [Officer] This is
now effectively a riot.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.650
- [Narrator] Testimony
from Capitol police officer

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.950
Caroline Edwards, described
the attacks as a war scene.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.830
- I saw friends with blood
all over their faces.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.560
I was slipping in people's blood.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.810
- The goal of that was to really show

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.310
to the American public,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.760
many of whom may not have
seen footage like this before,

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.500
how violent it was.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.570
- [Narrator] Steven Ayres,
a former Trump supporter

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.490
who pleaded guilty to
breaching the Capitol,

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.800
testified that he
initially had no intention

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.210
of going there on the sixth.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.600
- Basically, you know,
the president, you know,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.470
got everybody riled up, told
everybody to head on down.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.560
So we basically were just
following what he said.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.910
- [Narrator] Video showed rioters reading

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.800
a Tweet sent by Trump that criticized

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.540
then vice president Mike Pence,

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.120
for refusing to block the
electoral college count.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.490
- [Man Over PA] Mike Pence
didn't have the courage to do

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.395
what should have been done to protect

00:03:31.395 --> 00:03:34.230
our country and our constitution.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.160
- [Narrator] The committee detailed

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.870
the potential peril to Pence,

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.130
who became a clear target of the mob.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.726
- [Man Over PA] Bring out Pence.

00:03:41.726 --> 00:03:43.230
Bring out Pence.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.250
- [Narrator] The crowds surged,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.110
and within one minute of Trump's Tweet

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.850
made it to one floor below where Pence

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.450
was waiting off the Senate floor

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.560
- [Officer] Vice president
Pence and his team

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.860
ultimately were led to a secure location

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.520
where they stayed for the
next four and a half hours,

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.670
barely missing rioters a few feet away.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.140
- The main point that the committee

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.310
was trying to make with this

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.670
is how Trump has this
power over his followers,

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.253
and they do what he
says and he knows that.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.630
- [Narrator] According to
videotaped depositions,

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.150
Trump was told repeatedly
by top Justice Department

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.400
officials and members of his inner circle

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.500
that he hadn't won the 2020 election.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.200
And that claims a voter
fraud were without merit.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.000
- [William] I told him
that it was crazy stuff.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.080
- [Narrator] Trump continued to spread

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.430
election fraud claims,

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.380
including ones that election workers

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.330
brought a suitcase full of fake ballots

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.640
into an Atlanta voting facility.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.380
- Evidence of fraud is overwhelming.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.390
And again, I'm gonna ask you to look up

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:45.900
at that very very powerful
and very expensive screen.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:49.560
- [Anchor] Hidden cases of
possible ballots are rolled out

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.940
from under a table, four people
under a cloud of suspicion.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:54.870
- [Narrator] Gabriel Sterling,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.150
a top Republican Georgia election official

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.430
addressed the claims in
testimony to the committee.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.830
- What it actually
showed was Fulton County

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.280
election workers engaging
in normal ballot processing.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.320
- [Narrator] Testimony from
Georgia's Secretary of State,

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.170
Brad Raffensperger detailed
requests by Trump aimed

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.150
at overturning the election results.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.640
- [Donald Trump] Look,
all I wanna do is this.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.060
I just wanna find

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.430
11,780 votes

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.880
which is one more that we
have because we won the state.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.500
- There were no votes to find.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.590
That was an accurate count
that had been certified.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.430
- [Narrator] Ruby Freeman,

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.170
who was a Georgia election worker

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.540
also testified about
how she received threats

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.210
so severe that at one
point she went into hiding

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:42.600
after Trump accused her of
participating in voter fraud.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.233
- There is nowhere I feel safe, nowhere.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.890
Do you know how it feels
to have the president

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.263
of the United States to target you?

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.170
- [Narrator] the public hearings laid out

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.150
the committee's view of
the attack on the Capitol

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:03.570
as a watershed historical
moment for American democracy,

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:06.570
and a red alarm for threats
it could face in the future.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.100
- [Scott] What they're saying is

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.610
that they continue to
hear from new witnesses.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.690
We don't know who these people are?

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:13.860
But we're being told

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.800
that there's enough to
merit further hearings.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.510
- [Narrator] Members of
the January 6th Committee

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.580
have indicated they
believe Trump broke the law

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.900
when he attempted to overturn

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.850
the 2020 presidential election.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:27.180
But they have no power to
initiate a criminal investigation.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.230
- They can't make charges.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.670
That's not their role.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.257
But it is the role of the DOJ.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.340
- [Narrator] The Justice Department

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.800
is conducting its own
parallel investigation into

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.360
the January 6th attack.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.770
- We are seeing signs

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.320
that the investigation is widening,

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.180
and potentially looking

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.940
at individuals in Trump's inner circle.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.250
Although as of yet we don't have any sign

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.403
that the DOJ is looking
at Mr. Trump himself.

00:06:51.831 --> 00:06:53.405
- [Man] This way!

00:06:53.405 --> 00:06:54.238
This way!

